woocommerce	connection	wp_2_options		medium	0	The copy keeps the live site's Jetpack connection; connected services would act for the live site	Disconnect the copy: delete the blog token in jetpack_private_options and the auth entry in woocommerce_helper_data, or define JETPACK_STAGING_MODE in its wp-config.php	act as the live site	The copy keeps the live site's Jetpack connection
woocommerce	email	wp_2_options		high	1	1 WooCommerce Memberships email is enabled; staging would send it to members, for example when a membership ends	Turn these emails off in WooCommerce > Settings > Emails in the copy, or route mail to a catcher such as Mailpit	email members	1 WooCommerce Memberships email is enabled
woocommerce	email	wp_2_options	woocommerce_new_order_settings	medium	0	WooCommerce emails store staff about new, cancelled and failed orders; staging would email them too	Set these emails to off in WooCommerce > Settings > Emails in the copy, or route mail to a catcher such as Mailpit	email store staff	WooCommerce emails store staff about new, cancelled and failed orders
wordpress	email	wp_options		medium	4	4 plugin settings on 2 sites send notification emails to staff addresses (for example fixture_a_recipient, fixture_admin_recipient, fixture_b_recipient)	Point these settings at a test address, or route mail to a catcher such as Mailpit, in the copy	email staff	4 plugin settings on 2 sites send notification emails to staff addresses (for example fixture_a_recipient, fixture_admin_recipient, fixture_b_recipient)
wordpress	email	wp_sitemeta	wp_mail_smtp	high	0	Outgoing email of the whole network is sent through WP Mail SMTP	Point the mailer at a mail catcher such as Mailpit, or turn it off, in the copy	send email	Outgoing email of the whole network is sent through WP Mail SMTP
wordpress	scheduled_jobs	wp_options	cron	low	407	at least 407 WP-Cron events would run on staging (most common: fixture_cleanup (407))	Turn cron off on the copy's host (DISABLE_WP_CRON stops runs on page loads, not a system cron), and change the plugins' own settings, since they schedule their events again	run cron events	at least 407 WP-Cron events would run on staging
